description: PostgreSQL schema and migration rules
alwaysApply: false
globs: "apps/api/**/*.{ts,sql}"
Database Rules

PostgreSQL is the primary database.

Before changing schema:

Read docs/DATABASE.md.
Inspect existing entities/models.
Inspect existing migrations.
Identify relationships.
Create a new migration.
Add tests where appropriate.
Update documentation if architecture changed.

Never edit an already-applied migration.

Never silently drop data.

Never create duplicate tables because a similar entity exists.

Use foreign keys where appropriate.

Use unique constraints for business invariants.

Add indexes based on actual query requirements.

Avoid N+1 queries.

Use transactions for atomic operations.

Money must use decimal-safe representation.

Do not use floating-point numbers for monetary values.

Use a consistent timezone strategy.

Never put secrets in migrations or source code.